@startuml
' SPDX-License-Identifier: LicenseRef-Nordic-5-Clause
' Modules and the zbus channels they communicate over. Private channels are
' left out; see ../architecture.md#private-channels.
!include style.puml

component "Network module" as Network
component "Main module" as Main
component "Cloud module" as Cloud
component "FOTA module" as Fota
component "Location module" as Location
component "Modem AT module" as ModemAt #FFFFFF;line:94A3B8;line.dashed
rectangle "Host shell" as Shell #FFFFFF;line:94A3B8;line.dashed

Network -down-> Main : network_chan:\nconnectivity status
Main -up-> Network : network_chan:\nconnect, disconnect

Main -down-> Cloud : cloud_chan:\nconnect, send message, poll shadow,\npost Memfault data, resolve position
Cloud -up-> Main : cloud_chan:\nconnection status

Main -down-> Fota : fota_chan:\npoll, cancel
Fota -up-> Main : fota_chan:\njob status, reboot request

Main -down-> Location : location_chan:\nsearch trigger
Location -up-> Main : location_chan:\nsearch status,\nWi-Fi scan result

Shell -[#94A3B8,dashed]down-> ModemAt : modem_at_run()

legend bottom
  Every module owns one channel, and both the requests sent to a module and the
  notifications it publishes go on that channel. All communication passes through the
  Main module, the only module that knows about the others. The Modem AT module is
  outside the message graph: it serializes access to the modem AT pipe and is called
  directly from the host shell.
end legend

@enduml
